    "body": "The `shells` field was changed from private to `pub(crate)` solely to allow the test in `tests/manager_tests.rs` (line 167) to access it. This widens the API surface of `PersistentShellManager` for the entire crate, not just tests. A more targeted approach would be to add a `#[cfg(test)]` helper method (e.g., `pub(crate) async fn shell_count(&self) -> usize`) on `PersistentShellManager`, similar to the `inject_pending_readiness_for_test` pattern in `service_proxy_manager/test_helpers.rs`. This keeps the field private while still enabling test assertions.",
